# .claude/reconcile.config — terms whose presence in memory files signals drift.
#
# session-end.sh (the SessionEnd hook) greps memory files under
# ~/.claude/projects/<project>/memory/ for these patterns and warns if any
# are found. Use to track:
#   - Removed infrastructure (e.g. "ioredis" after dropping Redis)
#   - Renamed services (e.g. "old-service-name" after a rename)
#   - Deprecated libs whose mentions in memory should be cleaned up
#
# Format: one ERE (extended regex) pattern per line.
# Lines starting with `#` are comments. Blank lines are ignored.
#
# Copy to `.claude/reconcile.config` and add patterns specific to this project.
# An empty config is valid — it just disables the stale-term check.
#
# Example (uncomment + edit):
# old-service-name
# legacy\.api\.example\.com
# DeprecatedClient
